  "finding": "The inherited S35 parent imports psutil inside parent(), so the derived bytecode stores it as a fast local. V6 spawn_worker instead asks the separate derived module namespace for namespace['psutil'] at both the normal watchdog call and its cleanup path. No write places that local into the module namespace. The watchdog therefore enters a KeyError path before its production monitor can run, and the cleanup lookup repeats the same failure.",
  "minimum_required_fix": "The AST-derived subprocess.Popen replacement must pass the parent-local psutil value explicitly as a required process_api keyword to the private spawn_worker closure; normal watchdog monitoring and exceptional cleanup must use that same required binding. Add a disposable regression that traverses the actual derived parent to the private spawn and watchdog boundary.",
